summary.example:
This example shows how to get an instance of type  using the composition root :

using var composition = new KuGouComposition(_argSessionPersistence316d, _argCookieContainer316d, _argLoggerFactory316d);
var instance = composition.Root;

See also:

This example shows how to get an instance of type :

using var composition = new KuGouComposition(_argSessionPersistence316d, _argCookieContainer316d, _argLoggerFactory316d);
var instance = composition.Root;

member.summary:
Defines how instances are created and reused within a composition.
Binding as Singleton:
DI.Setup("Composition") .Bind<IDependency>().As(Lifetime.Singleton).To<Dependency>();

Creates a new instance for each injection (default behavior). Default behavior can be changed by and .
Explicit transient binding:
DI.Setup("Composition") .Bind<IDependency>().As(Lifetime.Transient).To<Dependency>();
Default behavior (equivalent):
DI.Setup("Composition") .Bind<IDependency>().To<Dependency>();

Maintains a single instance per composition instance (singleton within the composition).
Singleton binding:
DI.Setup("Composition") .Bind<IService>().As(Lifetime.Singleton).To<Service>();

Single instance per composition root resolution.
Per-resolve binding:
DI.Setup("Composition") .Bind<IProcessor>().As(Lifetime.PerResolve).To<Processor>();

Reuses instances within generated code blocks to reduce allocations.
Per-block binding:
DI.Setup("Composition") .Bind<ILogger>().As(Lifetime.PerBlock).To<Logger>();

Single instance per scope.
Scoped binding:
DI.Setup("Composition") .Bind<IDatabase>().As(Lifetime.Scoped).To<Database>();

Provides configuration hints for fine-tuning code generation behavior.


// Resolve = Off
DI.Setup("Composition")
    .Bind<IDependency>().To<Dependency>();

or using the API call :

DI.Setup("Composition")
    .Hint(Hint.Resolve, "Off")
    .Bind<IDependency>().To<Dependency>();

